faq:
  - q: What is a dispatch fee usually charged on?
    a: Many agreements use a percentage of the load. The important question is whether that percentage applies to linehaul only, or to gross revenue including fuel surcharge and other accessorials. The contract should say so in writing. This calculator lets you compare both, using numbers you enter.
  - q: What does the break-even raise mean?
    a: If you pay a percentage fee, you keep less than the gross unless the booked amount rises enough to cover the fee. The raise shown here is the increase needed on the figures the fee is charged on, so that what you keep matches the starting amount. It is arithmetic, not a forecast of what a dispatcher will negotiate.
